# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Robot Registration Client — environment configuration
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file:       cp .env.example .env
#   2. Edit .env with your values
#   3. Place .env in the SAME folder as client_robot.py
#      (e.g.  /home/ritesh/FMS_Codes/.env)
#   4. Run the script normally — it auto-loads .env at startup.
#
# NOTE: Real OS environment variables always take priority over .env values.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Config file path ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the assigned robot_id is persisted between reboots.
# Default: /home/<user>/.robot_config
#
# Uncomment and change the path below to use a custom location:
ROBOT_REGISTRATION_CONFIG=/home/ritesh/FMS_Codes/robot_config_file.txt

# ── MAC address override ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Use this ONLY when the auto-detection fails (e.g. unusual interface names).
# Format: colon-separated hex pairs (case-insensitive)
#
# ROBOT_MAC_ADDRESS=AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF

# ── Hostname override ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default: system hostname from socket.gethostname()
#
# ROBOT_HOSTNAME=my-robot-01

# ── Robot topic namespace ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by diff_motor_fms.py to subscribe to /<ROBOT_ID>/cmd_vel
# Example: if ROBOT_ID=robot_1 then topic = /robot_1/cmd_vel
#
# ROBOT_ID=robot_1
